# Line endings.
#
# Git stores LF and hands Windows checkouts CRLF, which is right for source but
# WRONG for the two kinds of file below — and wrong in a way that produces no
# error message, only something that quietly stops working.

# Shell scripts must keep LF. `sh` reads a CRLF script as a shebang ending in a
# carriage return and fails with "no such file or directory" naming a file that
# is plainly there. tool/hooks/pre-push is the guard that stops a push landing
# straight on main — a guard that silently stops running is worse than no guard,
# because nobody notices until something is already on main.
*.sh          text eol=lf
tool/hooks/*  text eol=lf

# The compiled calculation layer. Its staleness gate hashes the DART sources
# with line endings normalised (tool/gen-calc-js.mjs), so CRLF here would not
# break the check — but this file is generated on one machine and read on
# another, and a checkout that rewrites 92 KB of it produces a diff nobody
# asked for every time the platform changes.
site/lib/generated/radar-calc.js  text eol=lf
